@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build] pinned-package-input
Guest, host-tool and release derivations MUST use the supplied pinned Nixpkgs
input. They MUST NOT fetch an unpinned channel or use host-installed runtime
libraries as build inputs. See ADR-0011 and ADR-0030.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build] runtime-version-consistency
The exported Elixir and Erlang packages MUST match `.tool-versions` and every
project's runtime gate, including OTP patch level. Both packages MUST retain
the debug information required by Dialyzer. See ADR-0002.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:deployment] release-runtime-closure
A release bundle MUST include the application's release executable and metadata
identifying its pinned platform and runtime. Lilly bundles MUST also retain Nix
references to host tools, unshare and the static Firecracker/jailer pair
so exporting the recursive closure supplies those runtime dependencies.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:storage] zfs-only-provisioner-pools
Provisionable Lilly pools MUST require native ZFS GUID identity and MUST NOT
accept the retired logical budget (ADR-0159). Missing configuration MUST NOT
select ext4 or another backend.
Guest ext4 image generation and unrelated host root filesystems remain independent.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;deployment] signed-nix-cache-custody
Every Nix-enabled machine MUST configure the Overalls Cachix substituter with
the reviewed public signing key, retain the NixOS substituter, and require
signature verification. Cache credentials and signing private keys MUST NOT
enter Nix configuration or any machine image.
